.SH "NAME"
pcre2_get_error_message \- get textual error message for error number
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_get_error_message\fP\f(CR(int\fP \f(CIerrorcode\fP\f(CR, PCRE2_UCHAR *\fP\f(CIbuffer\fP\f(CR,
                            PCRE2_SIZE\fP \f(CIbufflen\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function provides a textual error message for each PCRE2 error code.
Compilation errors are positive numbers; UTF formatting errors and matching
errors are negative numbers. The arguments are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 10
\f(CIerrorcode\fP
.ad l
an error code (positive or negative), or zero for no error
.TP 10
\f(CIbuffer\fP
.ad l
where to put the message; may be \f(CBNULL\fP only when \f(CIbufflen\fP is zero
.TP 10
\f(CIbufflen\fP
.ad l
the length of the buffer (code units)
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The function returns the length of the message in code units, excluding the
trailing zero, or the negative error code \f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY\fP if the buffer is
too small. In this case, the returned message is truncated (but still with a
trailing zero, assuming \f(CIbufflen\fP is not zero).
With a recognized code and zero capacity, no output is written and
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY\fP is returned.
.sp
If \f(CIerrorcode\fP is neither zero nor a recognized error code
number, the negative value \f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA\fP is returned without changing
the buffer, even when \f(CIbufflen\fP is zero.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.